  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Pancreozymin (cholecystokinin, CCK-33) is a diagnostic agent used in tests of pancreatic function. DrugBank lists it as approved, investigational and withdrawn, so its current availability is unclear; it appears to be little used today.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27075779&quot;>Wikidata Q27075779</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>pancreozymin (cholecystokinin)</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>V04CK02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB08862&quot;>DB08862</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27075779&quot;>Q27075779</a></td></tr></table></body></html>"));
